For this sprint, our group succesfully implemented all required functionality. We did many things well: we reviewed pull requests shortly after they were added, we gave feedback when necessary, and we worked together to identify bugs, unresolved issues, and lacking functionality throughout the project. However, there are some things that we can do better going into next sprint. This sprint, a lot of the work and bug fixes were not finished until the day that the sprint was due. Next sprint, we should work to finish the project before the last day, and use the last couple days for final checks and documentation instead. We should continue to prompty review pull requests, communicate, and create issues when they pop up. Overall, we did well on communication and completed required functionality, but can improve by getting more of the work done early. 
